Jesus sends the twelve disciples.
Jesus called his twelve disciples to join him. He gave them authority to cast out demons and heal every disease and affliction.
Here are the names of the twelve apostles. The first two are Simon Peter and his brother Andrew. Then comes James the son of Zebedee and his brother John.
The disciples are Philip and Peter, as well as Thomas and Matthew the tax collector. Two others are James the son of Alphaeus and Thaddaeus.
The last two are Simon the Zealot and Judas Iscariot. Judas is the one who will later betray Jesus to his enemies.
Jesus sent these twelve out with the following orders: "Do not go to the Gentiles, do not enter any city of the Samaritans.
Instead of that, go to the people of Israel. They are like stray sheep.
And don't walk, go and say this message: "The sin of Paradise is close."
Heal the sick, raise the dead, cleanse the lepers, cast out demons. You received freely, give freely.
Do not carry with you in your girdles gold or silver or copper.
Do not take a suitcase with you. Do not take extra clothes, sandals, or walking sticks. The worker should be given what he needs.
When you enter a town or village, look for someone willing to receive you. Stay at that person's home until you leave.
Upon entering the house, greet those who live there.
If this house welcomes you, give it your blessing with peace. And if it does not, do not bless it.
Some people may not welcome you or listen to what you have to say. If they do not, shake the dust from your feet as you leave that house or town.
What I am about to tell you is real. The Day of Judgment will be easier for Sodom and Gomorrah than for that city.
I am sending you out as sheep among wolves. Therefore be as shrewd as snakes and as innocent as doves.
Beware! The men will hand you over to the local courts. They will flog you in their temples.
You will be brought before rulers and kings because of me. You will be witnesses for them, and for those who are not Jews.
But when they arrest you, don't worry about what you will say or how you will say it. At that time, the right words will be given to you to say.
It will not be you who speaks, but the Spirit of your Father who will speak through you.
Brothers will deliver brothers to be killed. Fathers will deliver their sons. Children will rise up against their fathers and kill them.
Everything is going to hate you because of me. But whoever endures until the end will be forgiven.
"When people attack you in one place, flee to another. What I am about to tell you is the truth. You will not have finished crossing the towns of Israel before the Son of Man comes."
The pupil is no better than his teacher, and the servant is no better than his master.
It is enough for a disciple to be like his master, and it is enough for a servant to be like his master. If the master of the house is called Beelzebul, what will those who live in his house expect?
Do not fear your enemies. What is secret will be revealed. What is hidden will be brought to light.
What I tell you in the darkness, say in the light. And what is whispered in your ear, proclaim from the rooftops.
Do not fear those who kill the body and cannot kill the soul; rather, fear the one who is able to destroy both soul and body in hell.
Is not two sparrows sold for a farthing? And one of them falls not into the ditch without your Father.
Not a single hair on your head does he let go of, does he not count!
So do not be afraid, you are more valuable than many sparrows.
What about someone who says in front of others that they know me? I will also say in front of my Father who is in heaven that I know him.
But what about someone who says in front of others that they don't know me? I will say in front of my Father who is in heaven that I don't know him.
Do not suppose that I have come to bring peace to the earth. I did not come to bring peace, but a sword.
