But when the Son of Man came, he ate and drank like you do. And people said, "This man is a glutton and a drunkard, and a friend of tax collectors and sinners!" But wisdom is justified by her deeds." The cities that did not repent after the miracles were destroyed.
Jesus began to speak out against the cities where he had done most of his miracles. The people there had not repented of their sins. And he said:
Here is the translation of the provided text: How dreadful it will be for you, Chorazin! How dreadful it will be for you, Bethsaida! Imagine if the miracles that were performed among you had been performed in Tyre and Sidon. Then they would have repented long ago. They would have put on black clothing. They would have sat in ashes.
But I tell you: Tyre and Sidon will be more tolerable for you on the day of judgment than yourselves.
And as for you, Capernaum, will you be exalted to heaven? No, you will be brought down to Hades. If the miracles that were performed in you had been performed in Sodom, it would have remained until this day.
